I can't give you the intraday high from this data. FRED only publishes the VIX daily close (series VIXCLS, "Daily, Close"). It has no open, high or low values.

What the data does show for November 20, 2026:
- **The VIX closed at 35.89.** That was its highest close of the week, and the intraday high was at least that level.
- **It jumped about 7.45 points (+26%) in one day**, from 28.44 on Nov 19.
- **The week's closes were** 22.91 (Nov 16), 25.46 (Nov 17), 24.56 (Nov 18), 28.44 (Nov 19) and 35.89 (Nov 20). That's up about 57% from Monday.

**How I got this:** I searched FRED for VIX series, checked the VIXCLS metadata (which confirms it's close-only) and pulled the daily values for Nov 16–20.

**Where to find the intraday high:** Cboe's historical VIX data page (VIX_History.csv has daily high and low), or a market data source like Bloomberg, Refinitiv, Yahoo Finance or your broker.

Also note that VIX data belongs to Cboe, so using it beyond personal use needs their permission.